YoungsModulus

Young's Modulus

Young's Modulus is the ratio of the tensile or compressive stress applied to a material to the resulting axial strain of the material.

E = \frac{\sigma}{\epsilon}

where:

E [var. scal. YoungsModulus] is Young's Modulus
\sigma [var. scal. Stress] is the stress
\epsilon [var. scal. Strain] is the strain

